SUMMARY:Deadline: ETH AI Center Doctoral and Postdoctoral Fellowships 2027
DESCRIPTION:The ETH AI Center's flagship fellowship programme funds doctora
 l and postdoctoral researchers doing interdisciplinary AI research\, eithe
 r within AI foundations or between AI foundations and application areas\, 
 including safe and trustworthy AI. Fellows are co-supervised across ETH gr
 oups and join the AI Center's community. ELIGIBILITY: doctoral track needs
  a Master's in computer science\, machine learning\, statistics\, physics\
 , engineering\, applied mathematics or a related field\, completed by June
  2027\; postdoc track needs a PhD completed by June 2027. Two to three ref
 erence letters are required. Selection weighs research excellence\, interd
 isciplinary collaboration and impact orientation. APPLICATION: separate po
 rtals for the doctoral and postdoc tracks (linked from the programme page)
 \; deadline 27 October 2026 at 16:00 CET. Related CLS and ELLIS PhD tracks
  have their own applications.\n\nOrganisation: ETH AI Center\, ETH Zurich\
 nLocation: Zurich\, Switzerland. In person at ETH Zurich.\nAward: Doctoral
  fellowship: CHF 73\,100 (year 1)\, CHF 78\,300 (year 2)\, CHF 83\,500 (ye
 ar 3). Postdoc fellowship: CHF 92\,500 (year 1)\, CHF 97\,200 (year 2). No
  application fee.\nDuration: About 3 years (doctoral\, extendable by up to
  1 year) or 2 years (postdoc)\, starting around September 2027.\n\nMore: h
 ttps://ai.ethz.ch/research/phd-and-postdoc-programs.html?utm_source=artifi
 cialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://ai.ethz.ch/research/phd-and-postdoc-programs.html?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Zurich\, Switzerland. In person at ETH Zurich.
